{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And all the people saw.</b> This teaches that there was not among them a single blind person. And from where do we know that there was not among them a mute? Scripture says: ״וַיַּעֲנוּ כָל הָעָם״. And from where do we know that there was not among them a deaf person? Scripture says: ״נַעֲשֶׂה וְנִשְׁמָע״ (Mekhilta)." "<b>Saw the sounds.</b> They saw what is heard — which is impossible to see elsewhere." "<b>The sounds.</b> Those that issued from the mouth of the Almighty." "<b>And they trembled.</b> נוּעַ means nothing but trembling." "<b>And they stood at a distance.</b> They were driven backward twelve mil, the length of their camp, and the ministering angels came and helped push them back, as it says: ״מַלְאֲכֵי צְבָאוֹת יִדֹּדוּן יִדֹּדוּן״ (Psalms 68) (Shabbat 8)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :register {:flags {2 ["the Almighty"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:53:22.692012472Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}